# Tor configuration for ONIONLAB.
#
# Every line is either required for the hidden services to work or is a
# deliberate hardening choice. The hardening choices are annotated, because a
# torrc you cannot explain is a torrc you cannot trust.

# --- hidden service 1: the marketplace --------------------------------------

HiddenServiceDir /var/lib/tor/hidden_service/market
HiddenServiceVersion 3
# Public port 80 on the onion maps to the container's 8080. The target is a
# container name on the internal Docker network, so this connection never
# leaves that network and never touches the host.
HiddenServicePort 80 market:8080
# A second port serving the same content over TLS. Onion services do not need
# TLS for confidentiality, but operators frequently deploy it anyway, and a
# reused certificate or public key is one of the strongest cross-service
# pivots available. The collector must be able to see one.
HiddenServicePort 443 market:8443
# Rate-limit introduction attempts. Without this a single adversary can exhaust
# the service's introduction points and take it offline cheaply -- the standard
# denial-of-service against hidden services.
HiddenServiceEnableIntroDoSDefense 1
HiddenServiceEnableIntroDoSBurstPerSec 200
HiddenServiceEnableIntroDoSRatePerSec 25

# --- hidden service 2: the discussion board ---------------------------------
# A separate address on the same host, running the same software. This is what
# lets the lab demonstrate recursive discovery and cross-service correlation.

HiddenServiceDir /var/lib/tor/hidden_service/forum
HiddenServiceVersion 3
HiddenServicePort 80 forum:8080
HiddenServicePort 443 forum:8443
HiddenServiceEnableIntroDoSDefense 1
HiddenServiceEnableIntroDoSBurstPerSec 200
HiddenServiceEnableIntroDoSRatePerSec 25

# Refuse to run if a service is misconfigured in a way that would leak.
HiddenServiceNonAnonymousMode 0

# --- client side (used by the ANVESHAK collector) ---------------------------

# Bound to the container's own interfaces; docker-compose then publishes this
# to 127.0.0.1 on the host only.
SocksPort 0.0.0.0:9050

# This Tor instance exists to serve our own onions and to fetch them. It is not
# a relay and must never become one.
ORPort 0
DirPort 0
ExitPolicy reject *:*
ExitRelay 0
PublishServerDescriptor 0

# --- hygiene ----------------------------------------------------------------

AvoidDiskWrites 1
SafeLogging 1
Log notice stdout
